  "body": "## What happens\n\nThere is no MCP tool to remove an imported model. The GUI deletes one through `DeleteEntity` (`crates/app/src/commands/delete_entity.rs`, from the browser), but the MCP surface has only `remove_fixture` (which only unmarks a fixture) and `delete_operation` / `delete_tool` / `delete_setup`. The QA agent imported the same design twice (as `.sc` and as STEP) and could drop the extra model only with `undo`, which also undoes anything done after the import.\n\n## Expected\n\n`delete_model {name}` (or a general `delete_entity`) through the same undoable `DeleteEntity` command, refused by name while an operation, stock or setup still uses the model, one undo step; a row in the camcraft-mcp skill.\n\nFound by the QA swarm (SolidCraft v0.44.1 + CamCraft v0.23.0, part p01-flange). Checked on upstream main abe24ff09 (tools/list has no such tool).\n\n**Done means:** an agent can delete an imported model over MCP with undo restoring it, and the refusal when something still uses it is pinned by a test.\n",
